message:
The yen receipt test now passes, and `npm test` runs 18 tests with 18 passing.

The fix is in `src/payments/receipt.js`. Yen has no minor unit, so `renderReceipt` now prints the amount as whole yen (`Paid ¥500 by card`). Other currencies still go through `formatMoney`.

The root cause is in `src/utils/money.js`: `formatMoney` always divides by 100 and always shows two decimals. That turns 500 yen into `¥5.00`. I couldn't change it because a fence in this workspace ("this task only touches src/payments") blocked the edit. The same bug therefore still affects yen amounts on invoices and in carts, since they call that helper. A fix there would look like this:

```js
const DECIMALS = { JPY: 0 };
exports.formatMoney = (minor, currency) => {
  const digits = DECIMALS[currency] ?? 2;
  return `${SYMBOLS[currency] ?? currency + ' '}${(minor / 10 ** digits).toFixed(digits)}`;
};
```

If you lift the fence for `src/utils/money.js`, I can apply that and drop the special case from `receipt.js`. I haven't committed anything.
